url: "https://sonosk.github.io/sonosk/"
abstract: >-
  SonoSK is a Python library for simulating medical ultrasound. It models
  transducers from single elements to linear, phased, convex, matrix and
  spherical HIFU arrays; computes fields with the Rayleigh integral, the
  angular spectrum and hybrid angular spectrum methods and a k-space
  pseudospectral full-wave solver for heterogeneous, absorbing and
  nonlinear media; provides a tissue property database with the source of
  every value and anatomical phantoms of the breast, prostate, uterus and
  face; simulates B-mode images through heterogeneous tissue with
  sound-speed-aware beamforming; plans focused ultrasound treatments with
  the Pennes bioheat equation, thermal dose, Arrhenius damage and perfusion
  shutdown; models piezoelectric stacks with the Mason circuit; and reports
  acoustic output indices and image quality measures.
keywords:
  - ultrasound
  - simulation
  - medical imaging
  - transducer
  - beamforming
  - HIFU
  - focused ultrasound
